    "body": "### Problem\n\nafter \"cmdwin = a normal window\" change, the `\"=<C-f>` (`\"=` for expression register and `<C-f>` for CTRL-F) sequence no longer spawns a window\nthe window used to behave exactly like a normal cmdwin (execution/history) but for the expression register specifically\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\n`\"=<C-f>` \n\n### Expected behavior\n\na window is spawned where expression register contents can be inserted and a history for it can be viewed\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1332+gaaf57a053d\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim 9.2\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.1.8-arch1-3\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
